# Naija Hunt does not read any environment variables yet.
# This file exists so the convention is in place before the first one is needed.
#
# How it will work:
# - Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in real values there. `.env` and `.env.*` are
#   git-ignored (only `.env.example` is committed). Never commit real values.
# - Vite exposes only variables whose names start with `VITE_` to browser code.
#   Anything with that prefix is public to every visitor. Never put a secret in a `VITE_` variable.
#
# Planned, NOT implemented, NOT read by the code today (Supabase milestone). Placeholders only:
# VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
# VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-public-anon-key
#
# A Supabase service-role key must never be placed in this app or in any `VITE_` variable.
